process-exit-running.m on the machine's GPU: the program ends by C's exit
while a GPU process, or a target region, still waits on the GPU, and ends
with its status and its output, with no fault from the kernel.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-exit-running.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env sh -c 'timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu 2>&1; echo "exit status $?"' | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: %gpu-env sh -c 'timeout -k 1 60 %t2 region 2>&1; echo "exit status $?"' | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
CHECK:the waiter started: 1
CHECK-NEXT:exit status 3
